==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*6 [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 24~30 seconds<sup>720f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Chickful A]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The main difficulty of the stage is the Le'noir and the Chickful A: you don't really get much money at all after 2 minutes. Use 3-4 meatshields, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], a barrier breaker cat (like [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]]), [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or another hefty damage-dealing cat and 1-2 long ranged attackers like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]].

Upgrade your worker cat to level 4-5 in the beginning, begin to stall a fair distance (perferrably 800~1200 range) from the base, and use Pizza Cat and The Kitty of Liberty sparingly to get through the initial wave of Gories and UltraBaaBaas, as they will push hard if you mess up. Then, spawn your long ranged attackers and meatshield for 5 gruesome minutes. Eventually, everything should die.

Using Awakened Bahamut and [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can be difficult at times because the Kroxos spawn very frequently, but could be done if your timing is impeccable.

